problem:
Problem description
- There is a single leasing-planning period over a planning horizon $$\mathcal{T}$$, and the mall must decide how many stores of each type to lease.
- There are $$P$$ store types indexed by $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$.
- Each store type $$p$$ has:
  - an area requirement per shop $$a_p$$,
  - a minimum allowable number of shops $$\underline{q}_p$$,
  - a maximum allowable number of shops $$\overline{q}_p$$,
  - an expected annual profit per shop that depends on how many shops of the same type are leased, denoted by $$\pi_{p,q}$$ for feasible count levels $$q \in \mathcal{Q}_p$$.
- The mall has a total leasable area $$A^{\text{tot}}$$.
- Each shop pays a fixed rent share $$\rho$$ of its expected annual profit to the mall.
- The optimization goal is to choose the number of shops of each type so that the mall’s total rental income is maximized.
- The chosen number of shops for each type must be an integer.
- The total occupied area of all leased shops must not exceed the available mall space.
- For each store type, the chosen number of shops must stay within its allowed minimum and maximum bounds.
- For each store type, the rental income contribution must be based on the expected annual profit level associated with the selected number of shops for that type.
- A solution is represented by:
  - The integer decision variables $$x_p$$, where $$x_p$$ is the number of shops of type $$p$$ to lease.
  - The resulting total rental income $$Z$$.
  - Optionally, the implied income contribution from each store type, if needed for reporting.

Input Format
{
  "A_tot": {
    "description": "Total leasable area available in the mall",
    "type": "scalar",
    "unit": "area"
  },
  "rho": {
    "description": "Fraction of each shop’s expected annual profit paid as rent",
    "type": "scalar"
  },
  "P": {
    "description": "Number of store types",
    "type": "integer"
  },
  "store_types": {
    "description": "Array of store-type records indexed by $$p \\in \\mathcal{P}$$",
    "shape": "[$$P$$]",
    "items": {
      "p": {
        "description": "Store type index",
        "type": "integer"
      },
      "name": {
        "description": "Optional store-type label",
        "type": "string"
      },
      "a_p": {
        "description": "Area occupied by one shop of type $$p$$",
        "type": "scalar",
        "unit": "area"
      },
      "underline_q_p": {
        "description": "Minimum allowable number of shops of type $$p$$",
        "type": "integer"
      },
      "overline_q_p": {
        "description": "Maximum allowable number of shops of type $$p$$",
        "type": "integer"
      },
      "Q_p": {
        "description": "Feasible count levels for which profit data are provided for type $$p$$",
        "type": "array of integers"
      },
      "pi_p_q": {
        "description": "Expected annual profit per shop for type $$p$$ when the selected count is $$q \\in \\mathcal{Q}_p$$",
        "shape": "[$$|\\mathcal{Q}_p|$$]",
        "indexed_by": "$$q \\in \\mathcal{Q}_p$$",
        "type": "array of scalars"
      }
    }
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "store_counts": {
    "description": "Chosen number of shops for each store type",
    "shape": "[$$P$$]",
    "values": "$$x_p$$ for each $$p \\in \\mathcal{P}$$",
    "type": "integer array"
  },
  "total_rental_income": {
    "description": "Maximum total rental income achieved by the chosen store mix",
    "shape": "scalar",
    "values": "$$Z$$",
    "type": "scalar"
  }
}

